      "content": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Strict//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-strict.dtd\">\n<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\">\n<head profile=\"http://gmpg.org/xfn/11\">\n    <meta http-equiv=\"Content-Type\" content=\"text/html; charset=utf-8\"/>\n    <title>Making CRDTs Byzantine Fault Tolerant &mdash; Martin Kleppmann&rsquo;s publications</title>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen, print, handheld\" href=\"/css/typography.css\" />\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\" href=\"/css/style.css\" />\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"all\" href=\"/css/pygments-default.css\" />\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"all\" href=\"/css/ansi2html.css\" />\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"all\" href=\"/css/customizations.css?5\" />\n<!--[if lt IE 8]>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/css/ie.css\" type=\"text/css\" media=\"screen\" charset=\"utf-8\" />\n<![endif]-->\n<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" title=\"RSS\" href=\"https://feeds.feedburner.com/martinkl?format=xml\" title=\"Martin Kleppmann's blog\" />\n<script type=\"text/javascript\" async\n    src=\"https://cdn.mathjax.org/mathjax/latest/MathJax.js?config=TeX-AMS_CHTML\">\n</script>\n\n\n    <!-- Info on meta tags for Google Scholar: https://www.monperrus.net/martin/accurate+bibliographic+metadata+and+google+scholar -->\n    <meta name=\"citation_title\" content=\"Making CRDTs Byzantine Fault Tolerant\" /> \n    <meta name=\"citation_publication_date\" content=\"2022-04-05\" /> \n    <meta name=\"citation_authors\" content=\"Martin Kleppmann\" /> \n    <meta name=\"citation_pdf_url\" content=\"/papers/bft-crdt-papoc22.pdf\" /> \n    \n    <meta name=\"citation_doi\" content=\"10.1145/3517209.3524042\" /> \n    \n</head>\n\n<body class=\"wordpress\">\n    <div id=\"page\">\n        <p id=\"top\">\n    <a id=\"to-content\" href=\"#content\" title=\"Skip to content\">Skip to content</a>\n</p>\n\n<div id=\"header\">\n    <div class=\"wrapper\">\n        <strong id=\"blog-title\">\n            <a href=\"/\" title=\"Home\" rel=\"home\">Martin Kleppmann</a>\n        </strong>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n<div id=\"sub-header\">\n    <div class=\"wrapper\">\n        <div id=\"navigation\">\n            <ul>\n                <li class=\"page_item\"><a href=\"/student-projects.html\" title=\"Student Projects\">Student Projects</a></li>\n                <li class=\"page_item\"><a href=\"/contact.html\" title=\"About/Contact\">About/Contact</a></li>\n                <li class=\"page_item\"><a href=\"/supporters.html\" title=\"Supporters\">Supporters</a></li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n<hr class=\"divider\">\n\n\n        <div class=\"wrapper\">\n            <div id=\"content\">\n                <h1>Making CRDTs Byzantine Fault Tolerant</h1>\n\n                <p>Martin Kleppmann</p>\n\n                <p>\n                  \n                    <a href=\"https://papoc-workshop.github.io/2022/\">9th Workshop on Principles and Practice of Consistency for Distributed Data (PaPoC)</a>,\n                  \n                  \n                    Rennes, France,\n                  \n                  April 2022.\n                </p>\n\n                \n\n                <ul>\n                  \n                    <li><a href=\"/papers/bft-crdt-papoc22.pdf\">Paper (open access)</a></li>\n                  \n                  \n                  \n                    <li><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1145/3517209.3524042\">doi:10.1145/3517209.3524042</a></li>\n                  \n                  \n                  \n                    <li><a href=\"https://speakerdeck.com/ept/making-crdts-byzantine-fault-tolerant\">Slides</a></li>\n                  \n                  \n                  \n                  \n                </ul>\n\n                <iframe class=\"speakerdeck-iframe\" frameborder=\"0\" src=\"https://speakerdeck.com/player/392910792df1434a8fcb7d00a3c19792\" title=\"Making CRDTs Byzantine fault tolerant\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" mozallowfullscreen=\"true\" webkitallowfullscreen=\"true\" style=\"border: 0px; background: padding-box padding-box rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); margin: 0px; padding: 0px; border-radius: 6px; box-shadow: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2) 0px 5px 40px; width: 550px; height: 420px;\" data-ratio=\"1.3333333333333333\"></iframe>\n\n<h2 id=\"abstract\">Abstract</h2>\n\n<p>It is often claimed that Conflict-free Replicated Data Types (CRDTs) ensure consistency of\nreplicated data in peer-to-peer systems. However, peer-to-peer systems usually consist of untrusted\nnodes that may deviate from the specified protocol (i.e. exhibit Byzantine faults), and most\nexisting CRDT algorithms cannot guarantee consistency in the presence of such faults. This paper\nshows how to adapt existing non-Byzantine CRDT algorithms and make them Byzantine fault-tolerant.\nThe proposed scheme can tolerate any number of Byzantine nodes (making it immune to Sybil attacks),\nguarantees Strong Eventual Consistency, and requires only modest changes to existing CRDT\nalgorithms.</p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <div id=\"sidebar\">\n                <div id=\"carrington-subscribe\" class=\"widget\">\n    <h2 class=\"widget-title\">Subscribe</h2>\n    <a class=\"feed\" title=\"RSS 2.0 feed for posts\" rel=\"alternate\" href=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/martinkl\">\n        Site <acronym title=\"Really Simple Syndication\">RSS</acronym> feed\n    </a>\n\n    <div class=\"mailing-list-signup\">\n        <p>\n            To find out when I write something new, sign up to receive an\n            <a href=\"https://martinkl.substack.com/\">email notification</a>,\n            <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/martin.kleppmann.com\">follow me on Bluesky</a> or\n            <a href=\"https://nondeterministic.computer/@martin\">Mastodon</a>, or subscribe to the\n            <a href=\"http://feeds.feedburner.com/martinkl\">RSS feed</a>.\n        </p>\n\n        <p class=\"disclaimer\">\n            I won't give your email address to anyone else, won't send you any spam,\n            and you can unsubscribe at any time.\n        </p>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n<div id=\"primary-sidebar\">\n    <div id=\"book-promo\" class=\"widget\">\n        <h2 class=\"title\">My book</h2>\n        <p><a href=\"http://dataintensive.net\" target=\"_top\"><img src=\"/images/book-cover-small.png\"\n            style=\"border: 1px solid #ddd;\"\n            alt=\"Designing Data-Intensive Applications\" width=\"180\" height=\"238\"/></a></p>\n        <p>My book,\n        <a href=\"http://dataintensive.net\"><em>Designing Data-Intensive Applications</em></a>, has received\n        <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/23466395-designing-data-intensive-applications\">thousands</a>\n        of five-star reviews.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"widget\">\n        <p>I am an Associate Professor working on <a href=\"https://www.inkandswitch.com/local-first/\">local-first software</a>\n        and security protocols at the <a href=\"http://www.cst.cam.ac.uk/\">University of Cambridge</a>.\n        If you find my work useful, please <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/martinkl\">support me on Patreon</a>.</p>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n                \n\n\n\n\n\n<div id=\"secondary-sidebar\">\n    <div class=\"widget\">\n        <h2 class=\"title\">Recent posts</h2>\n        <ul>\n            \n              <li>07 Oct 2026: <a href=\"/2026/10/07/centre-for-cryptographic-trust-infrastructure.html\">Announcing the Centre for Cryptographic Trust Infrastructure (CCTI)</a></li>\n            \n              <li>08 Dec 2025: <a href=\"/2025/12/08/ai-formal-verification.html\">Prediction: AI will make formal verification go mainstream</a></li>\n            \n              <li>05 Jul 2024: <a href=\"/2024/07/05/pudding-user-discovery-anonymity-networks.html\">Pudding: user discovery for anonymity networks</a></li>\n            \n              <li>04 Jan 2024: <a href=\"/2024/01/04/year-in-review.html\">2023 year in review</a></li>\n            \n              <li>12 Oct 2022: <a href=\"/2022/10/12/verifying-distributed-systems-isabelle.html\">Verifying distributed systems with Isabelle/HOL</a></li>\n            \n            <li><a href=\"/archive.html\">Full archive</a></li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"widget\">\n        <h2 class=\"title\">Conference talks</h2>\n        <ul>\n            \n              <li><a href=\"/2026/12/09/opodis-keynote.html\">09 Dec 2026 at 30th Conference on Principles of Distributed Systems (OPODIS)</a></li>\n            \n              <li><a href=\"/2026/09/24/srds-keynote.html\">24 Sep 2026 at 45th International Symposium on Reliable Distributed Systems (SRDS)</a></li>\n            \n              <li><a href=\"/2026/07/12/local-first-conf.html\">12 Jul 2026 at Local-First Conference</a></li>\n            \n              <li><a href=\"/2026/03/17/qcon-keynote-geopolitical-risk.html\">17 Mar 2026 at QCon London</a></li>\n            \n              <li><a href=\"/2026/02/24/local-first-meetup.html\">24 Feb 2026 at Local First (LoFi) meetup</a></li>\n            \n            <li><a href=\"/talks.html\">Full archive</a></li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <hr class=\"divider\" />\n\n<div id=\"footer\">\n    <div class=\"wrapper\">\n        <p id=\"generator-link\">\n            <a rel=\"license\" href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/\"\n                style=\"float: left; padding: 0.3em 1em 0 0;\"><img alt=\"Creative Commons License\"\n                src=\"/images/creative-commons.png\" width=\"88\" height=\"31\" /></a>\n            Unless otherwise specified, all content on this site is licensed under a\n            <a rel=\"license\" href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/\">Creative Commons\n                Attribution 3.0 Unported License</a>.\n            Theme borrowed from\n            <span id=\"theme-link\"><a href=\"http://carringtontheme.com\" title=\"Carrington theme for WordPress\">Carrington</a></span>,\n            ported to <a href=\"https://github.com/mojombo/jekyll\">Jekyll</a> by Martin Kleppmann.\n        </p>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n    </div>\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js/vce701823e78c4301a35b7e07294d87301792088814092\" integrity=\"sha512-UKNk8GbxkABxKcXYuLkO16EleLGUkcvJWtpSNmExE0Too3ZaFAxTscNWEc1OdAv5/BikHawapSCaiD2XCmp+Bw==\" data-cf-beacon='{\"version\":\"2024.11.0\",\"token\":\"ff4e61c8dd38417ca880df455ea4e388\",\"r\":1,\"spa\":2}' crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
